<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
      Activity theme for the app window.

      Parent is deliberately the SAME platform theme the manifest pointed at before
      (@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar), so this changes exactly one thing —
      the window background — and cannot drift any other platform default. There is no
      values-night/themes.xml on purpose: the night variation is carried by the
      @color/gisti_window_background alias (:composeApp androidMain values/ + values-night/),
      which keeps the parent style byte-identical in both configurations.

      Why this theme exists at all: the platform Light theme hardcodes a WHITE windowBackground,
      and windowBackground paints (a) the cold-start starting window before the first Compose
      frame and (b) every pixel Compose does not cover. Under enableEdgeToEdge the content draws
      behind the system bars, so any uncovered sliver — most visibly the strip under the
      navigation bar — showed white on top of the dark app theme.

      Deliberately NOT set here: android:statusBarColor, android:navigationBarColor,
      android:windowLightStatusBar, android:windowLightNavigationBar. targetSdk is 36 and those
      window-color attributes are deprecated no-ops from API 35 on; bar icon appearance is owned
      at runtime by enableEdgeToEdge() in MainActivity. Setting them here would be dead config
      on modern devices and a second, competing source of truth on older ones.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Gisti" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/gisti_window_background</item>
    </style>

</resources>
